// A patch of thorns: a world-file entity of kind "thorns", a box of dark brambles. In the design
// they appear from the third chapter on, first at the edges and then everywhere, so a patch has a
// `min_chapter` and is only there (visible and harmful) from that chapter.
//
// They never end the run. Touching one pushes the player back to the last safe spot
// (GameRules), because the design says the player should never feel punished.
//
// Properties set on the entity in the world editor:
// - `half_extents` (vector): the box's half sizes, the same numbers as the entity's shape. The
//   game can't read a shape back from the engine, so the file says them twice.
// - `min_chapter` (number, optional): the first chapter it grows in; 3 when missing.
Thorns :: class {
public:
    entity: i64;
    center: lantern:::math:::Vec3;
    halfExtents: lantern:::math:::Vec3;
    isActive~ bool = false;

    Thorns~: (entity: i64) : entity(entity), center(lantern:::world:::Position(entity)),
        halfExtents(lantern:::world:::VectorProperty(entity, "half_extents")) { }

    // Shows the patch and arms it from `minChapter` on; otherwise it isn't there at all, and
    // since it has no collider hiding the mesh is enough.
    Grow~: (chapter: i32) -> void {
        minChapter := lantern:::world:::HasProperty(entity, "min_chapter") ? i32(lantern:::world:::NumberProperty(entity, "min_chapter")) : 3;
        isActive = chapter >= minChapter;
        lantern:::world:::SetVisible(entity, isActive);
        lantern:::world:::SetTint(entity, "5A1626");
    }
}
